[background arg="res://arts/splash art/backgrounds/galaxia.png" fade="0.0"]
In a dreamy state, I feel myself floating away in an infinitely expanding open space. I am surrounded by stars, galaxies, and everything is silent around me.
I see colors that I’ve never seen before. My body is naked, and the air is warm.
stranger: “I like coming here too.”
I didn't expect the voice that spoke to me. It caresses my ear, disembodied, making my skin crawl. I know now that there is somebody else with me here, only I can’t see them.
join alien (sonho/feliz e olho fechado) center
stranger: “I like coming here when things down there become too difficult”
\doctor: “...Who are you?”
stranger: “I am a visitor of this place, same as you.”
\doctor: “Of this dream, you mean?”
stranger: “Ah, so you’re sleeping right now? I have to make some conscious effort to come here, you see? Some people just slip up here unawares.”
\doctor: “Yes, I am sleeping. This is the first time that I have a dream like this.”
stranger: “It’s lucky then, that I found you here. I can show you my favorite views. Look over there, that pink spot on your left. It happens to be a galaxy that has been dying for millions of years."
stranger: "One day, its light will no longer reach us. But you and I will be long gone.”
\doctor: “That’s sad. I didn’t even get the chance to learn about it before it was gone. Now, I know I never will.”
stranger: “Do you have to understand something to appreciate its beauty?”
\doctor: “Yes, actually. The beauty is in understanding the intricacies of a thing, its in and outs. A mere surface level first impression can’t be actually called beautiful.”
stranger: “Is this place not beautiful?”
